# Go
/bin/
*.test
*.out
# stray repo-root Go build artifacts from an ad-hoc `go build ./<pkg>` (real builds go to
# package.nix / a temp dir), named after their cmd dir.
/driver
/briard-agent
/witness-forwarder
/reverse-proxy-bin

# Nix
/result
/result-*
/.direnv/

# editor / OS
*.swp
.DS_Store

# secrets — never commit (loaded via direnv dotenv; see .envrc)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/.secrets/
/token
# Binary-cache signing keys. `publish-cache.sh keygen` defaults its PRIVATE key to
# ./cache-priv-key.pem — i.e. THIS directory, which is the repo V3.7a publishes publicly, so
# an unguarded `git add -A` right after keygen would commit the trust root for every guest's
# OS updates. The real key belongs outside the tree entirely (point CACHE_SIGN_KEY at it);
# this is a backstop for the default path, not the plan. [B.74]
*.pem
cache-priv-key
cache-pub-key
